summary:
  The file the address is written into takes the session's default mode.

history:
  The address is kept off the command line because it can carry a token; a
  file other users can read gives it away just the same.

target:
  package/contents/ui/LoudLogic.js

find:
          write: ": LD_URL; umask 077; printf '%s' " + q(a.url)

replace:
          write: ": LD_URL; printf '%s' " + q(a.url)

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_loudlogic.qml::test_the_address_goes_into_a_file_and_never_to_the_helper.
  Line-neutral.
